-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Decision functions answer `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words (a flat negative, a "where", "if", "unless", "until" or "when" not met).
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer (a scope limit, a bare "must" not done, a list that is not closed, a lifted bar).
-- O 3 r 2(1) is a caveat on every answer (the Court may order otherwise in the interests of justice).
-- The Partnership Act and Orders 8, 22 are not among the sources: what they say is an input.
-- This Order fixes no period that is counted: r 2(1) says "forthwith", which is a judgment and not a count, so it is an input.
-- In this Order "the firm" is the name under which partners sue or are sued; the facts about who is a partner are inputs.

