      direction IS A `o 56 r 6(2) the direction`
      `the direction is just` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 56 r 6(2) the Court may give the direction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the Court is hearing an application under this Rule`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Court hearing an application under this Rule may give" is a "hearing" condition
        IF direction EQUALS `o 56 r 6(2) another direction as may be just`
        THEN IF `the direction is just`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "such directions including directions as to the taking of accounts and the making of inquiries as may be just" does not close the list, and the limit is "as may be just"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

