-- src:6780 | 7. —(1) An order may be made under Order 22, Rule 2 in relation to debts due whether immediately or at some future date or at certain intervals in the future from a firm carrying on business within the jurisdiction, even though one or more members of the firm is resident out of the jurisdiction. (2) A notice of attachment under Order 22, Rule 6 relating to such debts must be served on a member of the firm within the jurisdiction or on some other person having the control or management of the partnership business.
