    IF `the debts are due, whether immediately or at some future date or at certain intervals in the future, from a firm carrying on business within the jurisdiction`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the answer is the same whether or not `one or more members of the firm is resident out of the jurisdiction`: "even though"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule is "in relation to debts due ... from a firm carrying on business within the jurisdiction"

